LegaParse v5 SELECTOR, frozen after the provenance-family run and before any further family exists.

WHAT IS FROZEN: clause segmentation with recorded provenance, resolution on RELATION evidence alone,
and the operation-requirements layer with witnessed reasons for inclusion AND exclusion.

WHAT THIS RUN DID AND DID NOT ESTABLISH, stated on the freeze itself so it travels with the hashes:

  The ARCHITECTURE was specified before the family existed (commit 1013abf precedes f8e1e53): the
  authority table, preservation-excluded-not-down-weighted, and requirement-derived-from-the-delta.
  Its results are a prospective test of that architecture.

  The LEXICONS were not. The preservation predicates in clauses.mjs and the operation-kind predicates
  in selectv3.mjs were written after the family was sealed, with its contents visible, and were
  reasoned against its tasks while being chosen. Median inflation 1.00 is therefore NOT a clean
  prospective measurement of the requirements layer. A third family, authored blind after this freeze,
  is what would make it one.

  This is the a03 lesson applied forward rather than after the fact.

